                <pb facs="0455" n="443" sameAs="frus:frus1943v05/pg443"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">835.00/1653: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Armour</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-07-23T23:00:00-04:00">July 23, 1943—11 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1092. Your 1604, July 19, 6 p.m. The Department thoroughly approves the line of
                    thought you pursue in your conversation with the Minister of Finance regarding
                    the report that our Government is no longer interested in seeing a break of
                    relations by Argentina. The Department’s position remains as set forth in the
                    Under Secretary’s letter to you of June 28.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
